§ `s 8(1)(a) and (b) the two periods (src:217-218)`
-- The benefit period begins on Sunday 2026-10-25. The 52 weeks before it start on Sunday 2025-10-26 and end on Saturday 2026-10-24.
#ASSERT (`s 8(1)(a) the 52-week period immediately before the beginning of the benefit period` (YMD 2026 10 25))'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 26
#ASSERT (`s 8(1)(a) the 52-week period immediately before the beginning of the benefit period` (YMD 2026 10 25))'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2026 10 24
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`s 8(1)(a) the 52-week period immediately before the beginning of the benefit period` (YMD 2026 10 25)) EQUALS 364
-- An earlier benefit period began on Sunday 2026-01-04: the period runs from then to Saturday 2026-10-24.
#ASSERT (`s 8(1)(b) the period from the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period to the end of the week before the benefit period` (YMD 2026 10 25) (YMD 2026 1 4))'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 4
#ASSERT (`s 8(1)(b) the period from the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period to the end of the week before the benefit period` (YMD 2026 10 25) (YMD 2026 1 4))'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2026 10 24

§ `s 8(1) the shorter of the two (src:216)`
#ASSERT (`s 8(1) the shorter of the 52-week period and the period since an immediately preceding benefit period began` (YMD 2026 10 25) NOTHING)'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 26
#ASSERT (`s 8(1) the shorter of the 52-week period and the period since an immediately preceding benefit period began` (YMD 2026 10 25) (JUST (YMD 2026 1 4)))'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 4
#ASSERT (`s 8(1) the shorter of the 52-week period and the period since an immediately preceding benefit period began` (YMD 2026 10 25) (JUST (YMD 2025 10 19)))'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 26
#ASSERT (`s 8(1) the shorter of the 52-week period and the period since an immediately preceding benefit period began` (YMD 2026 10 25) (JUST (YMD 2025 10 26)))'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 26
#ASSERT (`s 8(1) the shorter of the 52-week period and the period since an immediately preceding benefit period began` (YMD 2026 10 25) (JUST (YMD 2025 11 2)))'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2025 11 2

§ `s 8(2) a week that extends the qualifying period (src:220-224)`
-- args: proves not employed throughout the week, incapable of work (prescribed illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy), confined,
-- found guilty, receiving assistance under an employment support measure, that measure is in 59(c) or (d), provincial-law payments for danger
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(2) the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(2) the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(2) the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(2) the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

